force","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T13:05:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T13:05:25Z","body":"I don't agree that ternary expressions are always better without a negation.\r\n\r\nI usually think about ternaries more in terms of:\r\n\r\n```\r\nQUESTION ? SPECIAL_CASE : DEFAULT_CASE\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo the \"special case\" is what relates to the \"question\", while the \"default case\" is what we'd have if there was no \"question\". \r\n\r\nIn this sense, I do sometimes end up with intentional negated expressions for the conditional. I can't say if this is the case for any of the code you are changing here, but I'd prefer to leave it as is to avoid accidentally masking code intention.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728839979/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728848626","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111611#issuecomment-3728848626","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111611","id":3728848626,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eQbby",